"""Advanced inventory, increment 2 (R104, design/advanced-inventory.md §6): physical counts.

Four new tables: inventory_counts, inventory_count_lines, inventory_count_entries (append-only) and
inventory_count_postings, with their guards.

Three tables are rebuilt, because each change lives in a CHECK and SQLite only changes a CHECK by
rebuilding the table, and each is rebuilt once for the increments that follow:

* ``inventory_movements`` admits the kinds ``found`` (quantity in valued by replay at the running
  average) and ``landed`` (reserved for landed cost), gains ``count_position`` (before, count or
  after; every stored row is ``before``, so nothing moves) and ``landed_on_movement_id`` (reserved),
  lets a ``found`` row capture a fallback cost, and lets a vendor return name its receipt in
  ``returns_movement_id`` (reserved for FIFO).
* ``inventory_documents`` admits the kinds ``count`` and ``landed_cost``.
* ``inventory_placements`` admits the position ``count``: a count's own difference sits between
  that date's documents placed before it and those stated after. It gains an index on
  ``sequence``, because what one command wrote is read back by sequence after every company write.

Every view and trigger is dropped and recreated around the rebuild, as co0070 does. DDL below is
frozen: this migration never imports current application metadata.
"""
